# Helpdesk — Project Memory

## What this project is
An internal helpdesk platform for support agents to manage tickets, powered by AI (Claude) for classification, summaries, and suggested replies. Tickets can arrive via email or be created manually.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Runtime | Bun |
| Frontend | React 19 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS v3 + React Router v7 |
| UI Components | shadcn/ui (Default style, Neutral theme, CSS variables) |
| Forms | react-hook-form v7 + zod v4 + @hookform/resolvers |
| Backend | Express 5 + TypeScript (runs on Bun) |
| Database | PostgreSQL via Prisma ORM |
| Auth | Better Auth (`better-auth`) |
| AI | Anthropic Claude API |
| Email | SendGrid or Mailgun |
| E2E Testing | Playwright (`@playwright/test`) — use sparingly |
| Component testing | Vitest + React Testing Library + `@testing-library/jest-dom` (jsdom via Vite) — **primary UI test layer** |
| Server unit testing | Bun test (`bun test`) — route/middleware tests |
| Rate Limiting | `express-rate-limit` (production only) |
| Client HTTP | **axios** (not `fetch`) |
| Client server state | **TanStack Query** (`@tanstack/react-query`) |
| Shared code | **`core`** workspace package (`packages/core`) — Zod schemas and types used by both client and server |

## Monorepo Structure

```
helpdesk/
├── e2e/                     # Playwright E2E — only for flows component tests can't cover
│   ├── global-setup.ts      # migrate deploy + seed-test on helpdesk_test
│   ├── global-teardown.ts   # Resets test DB on CI after suite
│   ├── helpers/             # auth.ts, tickets.ts, users.ts, inboundEmail.ts
│   ├── auth.spec.ts
│   ├── users.spec.ts
│   ├── tickets.spec.ts
│   └── inbound-email.spec.ts
├── playwright.config.ts     # loads server/.env.test; webServer on 8081 + client 5173
├── packages/
│   └── core/                # Shared Zod schemas + inferred types
│       ├── createUser.ts, updateUser.ts
│       ├── ticketEnums.ts, createTicket.ts, updateTicket.ts, listTickets.ts
│       └── inboundEmail.ts
├── client/                  # React app (port 5173)
│   └── src/pages/
│       ├── LoginPage.tsx, DashboardPage.tsx
│       ├── UsersPage.tsx, UsersTable.tsx, UsersPage.test.tsx, …dialogs
│       ├── TicketsPage.tsx, TicketsTable.tsx, TicketsPage.test.tsx
│       └── test/render.tsx  # renderWithProviders
└── server/                  # Express API (port 8080)
    ├── prisma/
    │   ├── schema.prisma
    │   ├── seed.ts          # admin user + sample tickets (dev)
    │   └── seed-test.ts     # admin + agent + fixture tickets (E2E test DB)
    └── src/
        ├── routes/
        │   ├── users.ts
        │   ├── tickets.ts   # GET list/get, POST, PATCH, DELETE
        │   └── webhooks/inboundEmail.ts
        └── middleware/
            ├── requireAgent.ts
            └── verifyInboundWebhookSecret.ts
```

- Vite proxies `/api/*` → `http://localhost:8080` (override in E2E via `VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET`)
- Run everything: `bun dev:server` and `bun dev:client` from root
- **`bun install` from the repo root** links workspaces; import shared schemas from `"core"`
- **`main.tsx`** wraps the app with `QueryClientProvider`

## Commands

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Dev server | `bun dev:server` (port 8080) |
| Dev client | `bun dev:client` (port 5173) |
| Component tests | `bun run test:client` |
| Server unit tests | `bun run test:server` |
| E2E tests | `bun run test:e2e` |
| Apply migrations | `cd server && bun run db:migrate:deploy` |
| Create migrations | `cd server && bun run db:migrate` (needs DB user with `CREATEDB`) |
| Seed dev DB | `bun run db:seed` |

## Implemented features

### Authentication
- Better Auth email/password; sign-up disabled
- `ProtectedRoute`, `AdminRoute`; role on session (`ADMIN` | `AGENT`)
- Login page; E2E coverage for auth redirects and role nav

### User management (admin)
- API: list, create, edit, delete users
- UI: `UsersPage`, dialogs, `UsersTable`; component tests + E2E CRUD

### Tickets — API
- `GET /api/tickets` — filter by `status` / `category`, sort `createdAt_asc|desc` (default newest first)
- `GET /api/tickets/:id` — ticket + replies
- `POST /api/tickets` — manual create (`createTicketBodySchema`)
- `PATCH /api/tickets/:id` — update status, category, assignee
- `DELETE /api/tickets/:id` — delete ticket (replies cascade)
- All ticket routes use `requireAgent` (ADMIN or AGENT)

### Tickets — UI
- `/tickets` route — `TicketsPage` + `TicketsTable`
- Columns: subject, status, category, requester, created
- Sorted newest-first via API (`sort=createdAt_desc`)
- **Component tests:** `TicketsPage.test.tsx` (loading, success, empty, error, sort param)
- **E2E (minimal):** access control, table display, sort order; creates cleaned up in `afterEach`

### Inbound email
- `POST /api/webhooks/inbound-email` — bearer secret; creates ticket or appends reply (threading via `externalMessageId` / `inReplyTo`)
- Shared payload schema in `core/inboundEmail.ts`
- Server unit tests: `inboundEmail.test.ts`; E2E API tests: `inbound-email.spec.ts`

### Database & seeds
- Migrations include email threading columns on `Ticket` and `Reply`
- **`bun run db:migrate:deploy`** (in `server/`) — apply migrations without shadow DB (use when `db:migrate` fails with P3014)
- **`bun run db:migrate`** — `migrate dev`; needs Postgres user with `CREATEDB` for shadow DB
- `seed.ts` — admin user + 4 sample tickets when table empty (dev)
- `seed-test.ts` — ensures admin, agent, and 2 fixture tickets (upsert by `externalMessageId`) for E2E

### Not yet built
- Ticket detail page (`/tickets/:id`)
- Create/edit ticket UI on the client
- Dashboard stats (still placeholder `—`)
- AI features, outbound email, knowledge base

## Prisma Models
`User` (id, email, name, role: ADMIN|AGENT, deletedAt)
`Ticket` (id, subject, body, status, category, priority, fromEmail, fromName, externalMessageId, aiSummary, assignedToId, createdById, replies)
`Reply` (id, body, isAi, sentEmail, externalMessageId, ticketId)

## Auth
- Better Auth configured in `server/src/lib/auth.ts`
- `emailAndPassword` enabled; public sign-up disabled
- `role` in `user.additionalFields`; client uses `inferAdditionalFields`
- Sidebar: Dashboard + Tickets (all agents); Users (ADMIN only)

